  "text": "\r\n\t\t Elections | Hampton, NH \r\n Skip to Main Content \r\nCreate a Website Account   - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.    \r\nWebsite Sign In \r\n\t\t\t Notify Me® \r\n     Town Departments   \t\t\t \n     Boards & Committees   \t\t\t \n     Community Outreach   \t\t\t \n     How Do I...   \t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t Search \nHome \nTown Departments \nTown Clerk \nElections \r\nElections\t\t \r\nNovember 3, 2026 State General Election Sample Ballot \n2026 State Primary Certified Election Results \nElection Information \n  Registering to Vote in New Hampshire  ( Register To Vote ) \n2026 ELECTION SCHEDULE \nNovember 3, 2026 –  State General Election  – Winnacunnet High School – polls are open from 7 am to 8 pm \nAbsentee Ballots \nEffective September 30, 2025 , voters applying for an absentee ballot will need to use the following instructions and forms on the link below and include the required  proof of identity (noted on the forms) when returning the application to our office.    No absentee ballot requests will be accepted without valid photo identification.   If you have any questions, please contact our office at (603) 926-0406. \nWe  CANNOT  issue ballots to anyone but the voter themselves (not even relatives or spouses). You can turn in their application with an appropriate copy of their identification, but  their ballot will be mailed to them. \nIf you submit an absentee ballot request in person and ballots  are not yet   available , your ballot will be mailed to you. If you submit an absentee ballot request in person and ballots  are  available , you will receive your ballot immediately.  \nThe deadline to request in person is 5:00 p.m. the day before the election. \nMail, email at townclerk@hamptonnh.gov or fax to 603-929-5917 your signed request form to the Town Clerk, along with a copy of your valid photo identification: \nState General Absentee  State General Absentee Ballot Application   \nLocal Election Absentee  2027 Town Absentee Ballot Application \nIf you are requesting Absentee Ballots for more than one election, you must complete a request form for each election. \nMailing Address :  Town of Hampton; Town Clerk; 100 Winnacunnet Rd; Hampton, NH  03842 \nFax:     (603) 929-5917   \nEmail to :   Townclerk@Hamptonnh.gov \nThe deadline to request an absentee ballot by mail is 12:00 p.m. the day before the election.  If you rely on receiving and returning your absentee ballot by mail, you should request your ballot more than two weeks prior to election day. \nDeadline for Absentee Ballots \nThe deadline for returning absentee ballots by the voter themselves in person or by the delivery agent is 5 p.m. the day (Monday) before the election.  \nThe United States Postal Service recommends putting your completed absentee ballot in the mail at least one week before the election.  \nWe will accept absentee ballots delivered to the polls by postal service or by a delivery agent (ID required) by 5 p.m. on Election Day.  \nAll ballots must be  RECEIVED  by 5 p.m. on Election Day to be counted. \nLook Up Your Voter Information or Absentee Ballot Tracking \nTo get more state voting information, visit the  Secretary of State's website . \nTo search for absentee ballot information, visit the  Absentee Ballot Search. \nTo check your party affiliation, use the  Party Affiliation Tool .  \nTo find a polling place, use the  Polling Place Search Tool. \nTo find clerk information, use the  Clerk Details Tool. \nTo view the state list of clerks & polling places, use the  State List Tool . \nMilitary & Overseas Voters \nFor detailed instructions and frequently asked questions, please visit the  New Hampshire Secretary of State's page for Uniformed and Overseas (UOCAVA) Voters . \nPlease reach out to the Town Clerk's Office for any assistance with UOCAVA voting. \nCitizen Petitioned Warrant Articles  \nNeeds to be signed by 25 or more registered voters in the Town of Hampton \nPetition Warrant Article Appropriated (fillable) \nPetition Warrant Article Non-Appropriated (fillable) \nGuidelines for Submitting a Citizen Petition (PDF) \n\t\t\t Directions \r\n\t\t\t Dog Licenses \r\n\t\t\t Elections \r\n\t\t\t Forms \r\n\t\t\t Motor Vehicle Registration \r\n\t\t\t Renewals \r\n\t\t\t Online Services \r\n\t\t\t Conducting business with the Town Clerk's Office \r\n\t\t\t Supervisors of the Checklist \r\n\t\t\t Town Moderator \r\n\t\t\t Marriage License Notice \r\n\t\t\t Agendas & Minutes \r\n\t\t\t Pay Online \r\n\t\t\t Hampton TV Channel 22 \r\n\t\t\t Trash & Recycling \r\n\t\t\t Property Information \r\n\t\t\t Employment \r\nContact Us \r\nThe Town of Hampton \n100 Winnacunnet Road \nHampton, NH 03842 \nPhone:  603-926-6766 \nFax:  603-926-6853 \r\nFrequently Asked Questions \r\n         U.S. Department of Homeland Security \n         American Red Cross \n         Ready.gov Website \n         Federal Emergency Management Agency \n/QuickLinks.aspx \r\nHelpful Links \r\n         Home \n         Site Map \n         Contact Us \n         Accessibility \n         Copyright Notices \n         Privacy Policy \n         Town Employee Email \n/QuickLinks.aspx \r\n   Government Websites by  CivicPlus® \nLoading \r\n\t\t\t\tLoading\r\n\t\t\t Do Not Show Again \r\n\t\t\t Close \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Left \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Right \r\n[] \r\n                     Slideshow Left Arrow \r\n                     Slideshow Right Arrow \r\n ",
